# Query filter field / operator constants

When building `QueryFilterConditions` (or `BaseQuery.addFilter`), do not hardcode field names or operator strings.

1. **Field** — use `<Entity>.Fields.<property>` from Lombok `@FieldNameConstants`.
2. **Operator** — use `Operators.*` (e.g. `Operators.EQUAL`), never `"eq"` / `"gte"` literals.

If the entity has no `Fields` nested type, add `@FieldNameConstants` to that entity and **tell the user** you added it.

```java
// ❌ BAD
filters.add(QueryFilterConditions.of("classroomId", "eq", classroomId.toString()));

// ✅ GOOD
filters.add(
    QueryFilterConditions.of(
        ClassroomInvoice.Fields.classroomId, Operators.EQUAL, classroomId.toString()));
```

Same for `BaseQuery.builder().addFilter(...)`.
